    "body": "@domenic I think you're correct that we should remove document's origin concept. We only ever make security decisions based on the global's origin. https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/410 is also about that.\r\n\r\nThe current browsing context restriction stems from 7eba67ebd8c89821c5dc25089eaebbc99839af14 and 7764ebcb0695587e5338576913b76db537272a5a which were made without sufficient research. It seems we should be able to remove that for the getter at least.\r\n\r\nFor the setter the situation seems similar, except that Safari did adopt throwing for documents without a browsing context, as far as I can tell.\r\n\r\ncc @bzbarsky ",
