    "updated_at": "2018-06-06T14:35:23Z",
    "body": "Okay, it seems that's how it works in Chrome too.\r\n\r\nIt seems that for the setter Chrome will validate any input, but only update the origin if there's a browsing context. Safari just throws early if there's no browsing context. So maybe the current specification of throwing when there's no browsing context is what we should try to align on, as that seems like a much more reasonable model.",
